From: Prithwiraj Samanta <app@datainsights.ae>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:10:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] telecode: resolve bundled assets against the app base

Under a sub-path base (/design/editor/) three things fetched from the origin
root and 404ed: canvaskit.wasm, the bundled Inter/Noto fonts and the brand
marks. canvaskit.ts already tried to honour BASE_URL, but guarded it with a
runtime `'env' in import.meta` check, which is always false in a production
bundle (Vite rewrites import.meta.env statically and leaves import.meta
without an env property), so it silently fell back to '/'. Add
bundledAssetURL(), which passes import.meta.env as a value the way
kiwi/fig/population/client.ts does, and use it for CanvasKit and the
bundled fonts; BrandMark uses import.meta.env.BASE_URL directly.
---
 packages/core/src/asset-url.ts     | 14 ++++++++++++++
 packages/core/src/canvaskit.ts     |  5 ++---
 packages/core/src/text/fonts.ts    |  5 ++++-
 src/components/brand/BrandMark.vue |  2 +-
 4 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 packages/core/src/asset-url.ts

diff --git a/packages/core/src/asset-url.ts b/packages/core/src/asset-url.ts
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..c2a7d144
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/core/src/asset-url.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+/// <reference types="vite/client" />
+
+// Vite replaces `import.meta.env` with an object literal at build time (in workers
+// too), so pass it as a value. A runtime `'env' in import.meta` check is always
+// false in a production bundle and silently resolves every asset against `/`.
+function baseOf(env?: { BASE_URL?: string }): string {
+  return env?.BASE_URL || '/'
+}
+
+/** URL of a file shipped beside index.html, honouring Vite's `base` (e.g. /design/editor/). */
+export function bundledAssetURL(file: string): string {
+  const base = baseOf(import.meta.env).replace(/\/$/, '')
+  return `${base}/${file.replace(/^\//, '')}`
+}
diff --git a/packages/core/src/canvaskit.ts b/packages/core/src/canvaskit.ts
